  "parentCard": {
    "title": "The pattern parade",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "sing",
    "steps": [
      "Tell them the job first: today they are the rule maker, and the whole family has to copy whatever rule they invent. Nobody argues with the maker.",
      "Show the shape once so they know what you mean. Clap, clap, stamp, clap, clap, stamp, sung out loud as you go. Then stop leading and hand it over.",
      "Let them invent their own parade rule with their body, whatever they pick: two claps and a jump, a pat and a spin. Sing it with them and follow them from room to room while everybody copies.",
      "Partway through, ask them quietly to break their own rule on purpose, once, without warning anybody. Let them be the one who gets to say caught you.",
      "Finish where they want to finish, then ask the question and wait: what was your rule? Let them say it in their own words, however they say it, and do not tidy it up."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "Does their rule stay the same all the way down the hall, or does it drift into a new one without them noticing?",
      "When they break it on purpose, do they enjoy the breaking more or the catching more?",
      "Can they say their rule in words, or can they only show it with their hands?"
    ]
  }
